/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  equil03_ammonia_oxidation_declared_pathways  --  a declared reaction that
                                                   runs to COMPLETION.

  The companion of equil02 (same shape, same lesson, a harder number).  Ten
  per cent ammonia in air, 1100 K, 5 bar, ideal gas, goes to three
  equilibrium reactors side by side; every answer is read as MOLE
  FRACTIONS, so the split is bookkeeping.

    gibbs     gibbsReactor over EVERY species (NH3 O2 N2 NO water): no
              reaction declared, the minimum of G under the N, H and O
              balances.
    declared  equilibriumReactor over ONE reaction:
                  ammoniaToNO   4 NH3 + 5 O2  <->  4 NO + 6 H2O
              and nothing else.  The N2 route (4 NH3 + 3 O2 <-> 2 N2 +
              6 H2O) is left OUT -- and with it every path to N2, including
              the decomposition of NO itself (2 NO <-> N2 + O2 is a
              combination of the two library reactions).
    complete  equilibriumReactor over both reactions: a COMPLETE set of
              independent reactions for five species over three elements
              (5 - 3 = 2).

  THE PREMISE IS YOURS.  Leaving the N2 route out states that, over the
  catalyst this reactor carries, ammonia burns to NO and neither ammonia nor
  NO finds its way to nitrogen.  That is kinetic knowledge; the engine
  cannot check it and does not try.  It computes what FOLLOWS from it.

  WHAT THE THREE ANSWERS SHOW (measured with this case, 2026-09-27):
    gibbs      y_N2 = 0.7424, y_NO = 6.78e-5, y_NH3 = 5.66e-18: with every
               pathway open, ammonia burns to NITROGEN and water.
    complete   the SAME outlet, every species to the last printed digit,
               NH3 at 5.66e-18 included: a complete set of independent
               reactions IS the Gibbs reactor.
    declared   y_NO = 0.0976, every mole of ammonia to NO (conversion 1 to
               the printed digits), and y_NH3 = 1.68e-14 left unconverted.
               Recompute it by hand from the declared equilibrium:
                 4 ln y_NH3 = 4 ln y_NO + 6 ln y_H2O - 5 ln y_O2
                              + ln(P/P0) - ln Kp,   ln Kp = 121.515

  WHY THIS CASE EXISTS.  ln Kp = 121.5 puts the unconverted ammonia near
  1e-14 of the outlet.  Until 2026-09-27 the equilibrium reactor solved for
  the reaction EXTENTS, so every amount was the feed minus a multiple of an
  extent, and a species that small is the difference of two nearly equal
  numbers; it also held every species above a floor of 1e-12 of the feed.
  Both the declared and the complete reactor here stalled ("Newton stalled
  at residual 16.26" and "69.77") and refused.  The unknowns are now the
  LOGARITHMS of the amounts (src/unitOperations/reactor/EquilibriumReactor.cpp,
  record docs/design/an-equilibrium-that-runs-to-completion.md), and 1e-14,
  or 1e-300, is an ordinary number for a logarithm.

  NOT here, and said: the NO -> NO2 oxidation downstream of the burner
  (NO2 is not in this species list), non-ideal fugacities, any rate, and
  any reactor that is not isothermal.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        split;
        type        splitter;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( feedGibbs feedDeclared feedComplete );
        operation   { fractions ( 0.5 0.25 0.25 ); }
    }
    {
        name        gibbs;
        type        gibbsReactor;
        in          feedGibbs;
        outputs     ( outGibbs );
        operation
        {
            T          1100 K;
            P          5 bar;
            elements   ( N  H  O );
            species
            (
                { name  NH3;    atoms  ( 1  3  0 ); }
                { name  O2;     atoms  ( 0  0  2 ); }
                { name  N2;     atoms  ( 2  0  0 ); }
                { name  NO;     atoms  ( 1  0  1 ); }
                { name  water;  atoms  ( 0  2  1 ); }
            );
        }
    }
    {
        name        declared;
        type        equilibriumReactor;
        in          feedDeclared;
        outputs     ( outDeclared );
        operation
        {
            T          1100 K;
        }
        reactions   ( ammoniaToNO );                // the N2 route EXCLUDED
    }
    {
        name        complete;
        type        equilibriumReactor;
        in          feedComplete;
        outputs     ( outComplete );
        operation
        {
            T          1100 K;
        }
        reactions   ( ammoniaToNO ammoniaToN2 );
    }
);
